Z||000011||loafer87gt||06-27-2001||06:07 PM||||I always bug my brother in jest about his Civic, but in all truth, I have never seen a Fiero with any engine swap go nearly as fast as some of those "Ricers" at the import drag races. Just recently, Stephen Papadakis 1.6 litre Civic ran 8.98 at 164 mph. You should watch the import vs. domestics car drags next time it's on speedvision. I gave imports a lot more respect after I saw Hondas, Toyotas, and Mazdas laying the smack down on 440 Chargers and the like. At the end of the day, the imports won the competition. The great thing about the imports is that they don't need 700 bazillion cubic inches to get decent power from an engine. This combined with their great gas milege and generally being more reliabile on a whole, makes them very appealing. I think things are looking better on the GM front now that they are starting to realize the virtues of smaller displacement OHC engines, and losing the bigger is better mentality that has plagued them for years. Front wheel drive, rear wheel drive, domestic or import, where all trying to get down the same track as fast as possible.  ||||reg||1
